60,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option A is a flat fee. It covers everything and is simple to collect.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option B is tiered. It lets people choose how much they participate.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option C is activity-based. You pay for what you use.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A seems best for the treasurer's workload. No chasing individual payments.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Option B might help newcomers who are afraid of a big commitment.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, I agree. The bank statements showed how hard it is to chase payments.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Kenji, but the minute books from named-grade years showed friction and exclusion.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, if we do tiers, the lower tier might feel like second-class members.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the ledger shows fixed costs are high. A flat fee ensures we cover them.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I worry about the quiet members feeling left out if we do tiers.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,I think Option A is the most fair and sustainable for the club's finances.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I am leaning towards Option A, but I am worried about the hesitation it might cause.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I prefer Option A because it simplifies things and doesn't penalize the active members.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I vote for Option A. It is the most manageable and reduces the burden on the treasurer.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I am torn, but I think Option A is the safest bet for keeping the club stable.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
